# Bleach bypass: the lab skips the bleach, so the silver stays in the print on top of the colour dyes. The result
# is a black-and-white image laid over the colour one: harsh contrast, muted colour, metallic highlights, dense
# blacks. Here that is literally what the graph does: a layer() with the colour picture at the bottom and a
# contrasty monochrome copy on top, blended with overlay at partial opacity (the strength of the "bypass").
#   colour        the bottom layer: the picture with a little less colour already, like the dyes under the silver
#   silver        the top layer: monochrome (saturation 0) ...
#   silver_curve  ... with a hard print curve, the silver image
#   layer(...)    overlay of the silver over the colour at 0.7: contrast up, colour down, like 70 % of the silver kept
#   recover       overlay on ACEScct code values pulls mid-grey down; put grey back where it was
#   steel         cool the shadows and mids a touch, keep highlights neutral: the steely look of war and crime films
#   grit          fine monochrome grain; the look is usually shot on fast stock
# Use it for war films, gritty crime and sports promos; dial the layer opacity for how much silver you keep.
cierra 0.1
name "bleach bypass"
about "Monochrome silver layer overlaid on the colour picture: hard contrast, muted colour, steely shadows."
input aces2065_1
output aces2(display: rec1886)

node colour = saturation(amount: 0.8)
  label "the dye image, a little calmer"
node silver = saturation(amount: 0)
  label "the silver image: monochrome"
node silver_curve = curve(points: [[0.0729, 0.0729], [0.28, 0.22], [0.4136, 0.4136], [0.56, 0.64], [1, 1]])
  label "hard print curve on the silver"
node recover = exposure(stops: 0.65)
  label "overlay darkens grey: bring it back"
node steel = wheels(lift: [-0.006, 0, 0.008], gamma: [-0.006, 0, 0.004])
  label "steely shadows"
node grit = grain(amount: 0.18, size_px: 1.4, chroma: 0, seed: 1971)

graph layer(colour, silver -> silver_curve, mode: overlay, opacity: 0.7) -> recover -> steel -> grit
